## Description
The Voter contract has a modifier `onlyGovernance`, which allows a function to be called if the caller is either the governor or the access hub. This means that the governor can bypass any timelock implemented in the access hub. 

Additionally, the `createCLGauge` function has a governor check for the main tick, making it callable only by the governor and not by the access hub:

```solidity
function createCLGauge(
    address tokenA,
    address tokenB,
    int24 tickSpacing
) external returns (address) {
    // ...
} else {
    require(msg.sender == governor, NOT_AUTHORIZED(msg.sender));
}
```

This creates a situation where the governor has unrestricted access, potentially undermining the role of the access hub and its timelock mechanism.

## Recommendation
Remove the governor's ability to call functions directly, ensuring all calls are routed through the access hub. Make the `createCLGauge` callable only by the Access Hub.

