## Description
The protocol is intended to be deployed to blast. In the blast network, the gas fee spent by the user can be claimed by the contract owner (see the blast building guides). Yet because all smart contracts do not set the gas mode to claimable and implement a function to claim the gas, those gas revenues are lost.

## Recommendation
```solidity
interface IBlast {
    // Note: the full interface for IBlast can be found below
    function configureClaimableGas() external;
    function claimAllGas(address contractAddress, address recipient) external returns (uint256);
}

contract MyContract is Ownable {
    IBlast public constant BLAST = IBlast(0x4300000000000000000000000000000000000002);

    constructor() {
        // This sets the Gas Mode for MyContract to claimable
        BLAST.configureClaimableGas();
    }

    // Note: in production, you would likely want to restrict access to this
    function claimMyContractsGas() onlyOwner external {
        BLAST.claimAllGas(address(this), msg.sender);
    }
}
```
For all contracts that will be deployed to blast, set the gas mode to claimable and implement a function to claim gas.

