## Deprecate Market Overview

## Context
Dahlia.sol#L465-L470

## Description
In the `deprecateMarket` function, we have the following implementation:

```solidity
function deprecateMarket(MarketId id) external onlyOwner {
    Market storage market = markets[id].market;
    _validateMarketDeployed(market.status);
    emit MarketStatusChanged(market.status, MarketStatus.Deprecated);
    market.status = MarketStatus.Deprecated;
}
```

Note that as long as the `market.status` is not `MarketStatus.None`, the owner can call this function repeatedly. This allows multiple `MarketStatusChanged(market.status, MarketStatus.Deprecated)` events to be emitted for the same market, which may be confusing for off-chain tooling.

## Recommendation
Although it's not necessary, it is recommended to impose a stricter check to ensure that this function can only be called when the market is either `Active` or `Paused`.

