## Update Asset Prices by Cega Function

The `updateAssetPricesByCega` function exhibits an ambiguous access control boundary which allows TRADER_ADMIN roles. The `updateAssetPricesByCega` function is used by admins to manually set the price information stored in the PendleAdapter contract. These prices are later fetched by the cega vault logic during settlement.

> _contracts/oracle-entry/adapters/PendleAdapter.sol_
```solidity
function updateAssetPricesByCega(
    uint40 timestamp,
    AssetData[] calldata assets,
    uint128[] calldata prices
) external onlyTraderAdmin {
    require(assets.length == prices.length, Errors.INVALID_ARRAY_LENGTH);
    for (uint256 index = 0; index < assets.length; index++) {
        address baseAsset = assets[index].baseAsset;
        address quoteAsset = assets[index].quoteAsset;
        uint128 price = prices[index];
        require(price != 0, Errors.NO_PRICE_AVAILABLE);
        assetPrices[baseAsset][quoteAsset][timestamp] = price;
        emit AssetPriceUpdated(baseAsset, quoteAsset, timestamp, price);
    }
}
```

Because this function includes an invasive feature which allows setting prices to arbitrary values, it shouldn't be callable by TRADER_ADMIN roles. The TRADER_ADMIN role is responsible for handling relatively permissionless actions such as setting the auction winner or collecting fees from the vault; it shouldn't be able to forcibly correct the settlement outcome of a vault. Therefore, we advise enforcing higher permission levels.

## Remediation

The Cega team created a new role, `SERVICE_ADMIN`, designated for this task.

