## Under the current implementation 

It is possible to call `initialize` on the implementation address. Calling `initialize` on the implementation contract effectively re-initializes the contract, setting the caller to owner and allowing the execution of methods with the `onlyOwner` modifier. 

## Remediation 

Prevent `initialize` from being invoked on the implementation contract by adding the following constructor to the proxy implementation contracts.

```solidity
constructor() {
    _disableInitializers();
}
```

