    streamId = LOCKUP_LINEAR.createWithDurations(
        LockupLinear.CreateWithDurations({
            sender: admin,
            //...
        })
    );
}
```

If the admin is transferred to a new address, any new claims will have the sender set to the new address, while the old streams will still have the old admin as the sender. Since the sender of a stream is unchangeable, this creates several potential issues:

1. **Stream Cancellation**: 
   As only the sender of a stream can cancel or renounce it, the new admin cannot cancel or renounce the old streams, and the old admin cannot cancel or renounce the new streams:
   ```solidity
   function cancel(uint256 streamId) internal {
       if (!_isCallerStreamSender(streamId)) {
           revert Errors.SablierV2Lockup_Unauthorized(streamId, msg.sender);
       }
   }

   function _isCallerStreamSender(uint256 streamId) internal view returns (bool) {
       return msg.sender == _streams[streamId].sender;
   }
   ```

2. **Withdrawals**: 
   Whenever the recipient withdraws from the stream, the `onLockupStreamWithdrawn()` callbacks happen to the sender at the time of the claim, which highlights the difference before or after the change of admin/ownership of the Lockup:
   ```solidity
   function withdraw( /*...*/ ) 
       try ISablierV2Sender(sender).onLockupStreamWithdrawn({
           // ...
       }) { } catch { }
   }
   ```

